Subject: client: add a module that decides when to ask for the window size

The client sends the window size to the guest once per size. When the
guest's display driver restarts, or Windows changes its resolution on its
own, nothing sends the size again, and Windows stays at the wrong size.

This patch adds new files only: client/src/resize.c, a pure state machine
that decides when to ask the guest for the window's size, and its unit
tests in client/tests/resize_test.c. The next patch wires it in.

A trigger (a new window size, a new display session's first frame, or a
change of the guest's size) that finds the guest at another size asks at
once, then after waits of 5, 10, 20 and 40 seconds while the guest still
differs, then stops. A change of the guest's size within 60 seconds of the
last ask continues that sequence, so a guest that keeps leaving the size
cannot cause a loop. No ask is made for a window under 640x480, the
smallest mode the IDD takes.

